.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-USERS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-users \- list Euclid user accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam list-users
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists user accounts via the eam service's
.I list-users
action. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1));
unlike
.BR euclid-cli-eam-register (1)
there is no bootstrap exception, since an empty user store has nothing to
list.
.PP
The JSON response, containing the matching users and the total user
count, is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only return users whose user ID starts with \fIPREFIX\fR. If omitted, all
users match.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of users to return. \fI0\fR or less (the default,
\fI\-1\fR) means no limit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index, applied when \fB\-\-page\-size\fR is set. Defaults to
\fI\-1\fR (meaningless while paging is off).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Field to sort by: \fIuserId\fR (default) or \fIemail\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, or the caller is not an
authenticated administrator. If the failure was an expired or invalid
session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
List every user:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-users
.fi
.RE
.PP
List up to 20 users whose ID starts with "jd", sorted by email:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-users \e
    --prefix jd --page-size 20 --page-index 0 --sort-column email
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-user (1)
